  Sixth architectural review corrections
  ☑ Clear native identity on existing texture wrappers when failed replacement cleanup deletes the
    new name. Preserve originating-context deletion, avoid double deletion after numeric name reuse,
    and verify both two-dimensional and layered replacement with and without a live registry.
  ☑ Make context-local metadata failure discard stale snapshots through manager-owned publication.
    Failed or interrupted refresh and failed image projection must not leave previous descriptors
    usable. Retain only the established texture target needed for explicit recovery; keep availability
    tracking out of both resource bases and introduce no parallel resource/lifetime registry.
    Validate context-local image selections before dependent use and verify recovery by native refresh.
  ☑ Have subagents add focused failure/recovery regressions and run affected tests and a forced
    Release/SPIR-V build. Reconcile documentation and review the final correction before closure.

