Phase 4d: Analyze binding-cache behavior and metadata acquisition queries
  Depends on Phase 4c. Analysis only; do not change runtime behavior in this phase.
  Sources: [proposal](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Proposal.md),
  [inventory](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Inventory.md),
  [API coverage](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.ApiCoverage.md).
  Findings: [per-method analysis](Rendering.GpuResourceHandles.Analysis.md).
  Outcome: each binding and acquisition path has an evidence-backed disposition for VGE-controlled
  resources. Analyze both responsibilities before deciding their shared architectural contracts.

  For every method task below, trace all production callers and downstream readers. Distinguish
  VGE-created/configured objects, external objects, raw-ID aliases of VGE objects, existing available
  entries, unavailable entries and context-local operation without a registry. Record native queries,
  their frequency/trigger, facts already supplied by VGE or available in canonical metadata, and the
  reason each query remains necessary or is redundant. A method named Acquire does not necessarily
  issue queries; report registry-only paths explicitly. Distinguish command inputs, established command
  results and driver-derived facts without assuming either blanket readback or blanket query removal.

  For each BeginNative/Complete pair, review the observation structure as well as its query policy.
  Establish whether work is required before execution, after execution or both; justify the captured
  token, original-entry identity and unavailable-state transition independently. Trace managed commands
  and intercepted external calls separately. Review native rejection versus managed exceptions,
  finally/completion behavior, secondary exception handling, context changes and interrupted updates.
  Determine whether readback, binding invalidation and resource revision publication are each needed.
  Treat this pattern as a review question, not a pre-established defect or a requirement to retain it.

  ☑ Analyze StateCache.UseProgramBinding: direct cache updates versus current-program readback,
    equal-binding suppression and the separate full-stage knowledge required by EXT selectors.
  ☑ Analyze StateCache.BindVertexArray: post-bind readback, known versus unknown selection, rejected
    selectors and the downstream effect on bound metadata commands.
  ☑ Analyze StateCache.BindProgramPipeline: post-bind readback and equal-binding suppression.
  ☑ Analyze StateCache.BindBuffer for ElementArrayBuffer: per-VAO cache invalidation, immediate
    recovery queries and preservation of metadata notification independently of binding knowledge.
  ☑ Analyze StateCache.VertexArrayElementBuffer: the removed NotifyVertexArrayElementBuffer cache
